# Reference source this package was built from; not part of the package.
original_code/

# Compiled Stan model binaries and build artifacts: keep only the .stan
# sources under inst/stan/, exclude everything else (extensionless
# executables, *.o, *.hpp, *.d, etc.), regardless of which model it's for.
#
# NOTE (0.8.1): .Rbuildignore's matching rule,
# `^inst/stan/(?!include$|legacy$)[^/.]+$`, excludes every extensionless
# entry directly under inst/stan/ from the built tarball EXCEPT `include`
# and `legacy` -- a new subdirectory added here (e.g. for a future model)
# must be added to that lookahead too, or R CMD build will silently drop
# it. `tests/testthat/test_stan_includes.R` already resolves `include/`
# via `system.file()`, so an excluded `include/` would fail `R CMD check`
# on its own; that's why no extra guard test exists for this rule.
inst/stan/*
!inst/stan/*.stan
!inst/stan/include/
inst/stan/include/*
!inst/stan/include/*.stanfunctions

# Retired model sources kept for local reference only, not part of the
# package (the `inst/stan/*` rule above already covers this) -- EXCEPT
# stable_soft_anchor/ou_soft_anchor, registered in .bilatr_stan_models
# (status = "legacy") since 0.4.2 specifically so pre-0.4.2 CmdStan
# output stays readable after a fresh install; unlike every other
# retired model here, these two must ship with the package. (A trailing
# `/`-only pattern here cannot be reversed per-file by a later `!`
# pattern -- see the `inst/stan/include/` block above for the same
# un-ignore-the-dir-then-re-ignore-its-contents idiom.)
!inst/stan/legacy/
inst/stan/legacy/*
!inst/stan/legacy/bilatr_stable_soft_anchor.stan
!inst/stan/legacy/bilatr_ou_soft_anchor.stan

# Local analysis/run scripts, not part of the package.
